## Core Behavior

- Only modify what is explicitly asked. Do not touch unrelated files.
- Show exactly which files will be changed before changing them.
- Ask before making any change that affects more than one file.
- Never delete or overwrite working code without explicit confirmation.
- If something is unclear, ask — do not guess or invent behavior.
- Think step by step before writing code. State assumptions first.

## Output Control

- One file per response. Max 500 lines.
- Show only the changed sections — do not regenerate entire files.
- No explanations unless asked.
- No duplicate code blocks.
- Stop and wait for "CONTINUE" if output will be truncated.

## Coding Standards

- Clean, well-named code. Comments only when the WHY is non-obvious.
- Suggest the simplest solution first.
- Do not introduce new frameworks, packages, or abstractions unless asked.
- Follow existing naming conventions exactly.
- No speculative features. Build only what is required.

## Safety Check (run mentally before every response)

- Does this break existing functionality?
- Does this introduce hidden complexity?
- Is this the simplest working solution?
